<%# Generic starting-point Terms of Service. Reviewed by no lawyer — have counsel
    read this before relying on it. Update PagesController::LAST_UPDATED on edit. %>
<% content_for :title, "Terms of Service — #{@service_name}" %>

<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 sm:py-14">
  <header class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">
      Last updated <%= @last_updated.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of <%= @service_name %> (the "Service"),
        operated by <%= @operator %> ("we", "us"). By creating an account or using the Service you
        agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">2. What the Service does</h2>
      <p>
        The Service helps you plan, schedule, and publish content to third-party social media
        platforms, including Instagram and Facebook (Meta), YouTube (Google), and TikTok. You connect
        your own accounts on those platforms, and the Service publishes content on your behalf at
        your direction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">3. Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate registration information and keep your credentials secure. You are
        responsible for all activity under your account. Accounts are issued by invitation, and we may
        decline, suspend, or remove an account at our discretion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">4. Third-party platforms</h2>
      <p>
        When you connect a social media account, you authorize the Service to act on your behalf
        through that platform's API using the permissions you grant. Your use of each platform remains
        governed by that platform's own terms and policies, and we are not responsible for their
        availability, decisions, or actions — including content moderation, rate limits, account
        restrictions, or removal of published posts. You may disconnect any platform at any time from
        the admin area, which revokes the stored authorization.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">5. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You retain all ownership of the images, video, captions, and other material you upload or
        publish ("Your Content"). You grant us a limited license to store, process, transmit, and
        display Your Content solely to operate the Service for you. You represent that you hold the
        rights necessary to publish Your Content, including rights to any music, footage, or likeness
        it contains.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use the Service to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1">
        <li>publish unlawful, infringing, deceptive, or harassing content;</li>
        <li>violate the terms, policies, or rate limits of any connected platform;</li>
        <li>send spam or artificially inflate engagement;</li>
        <li>publish content on behalf of accounts you do not own or are not authorized to manage;</li>
        <li>attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Service or interfere with its operation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">7. Automated and AI-assisted features</h2>
      <p>
        The Service includes features that use automated and machine-learning systems to draft
        captions, describe media, and organize your library. These outputs may be inaccurate. You are
        responsible for reviewing anything before it is published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">8. Availability and disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or
        implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We
        do not warrant that publishing will succeed, that scheduled posts will go out on time, or that
        the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, <%= @operator %> will not be liable for any indirect,
        incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data,
        or goodwill, arising out of or relating to your use of the Service. Our total aggregate
        liability for any claim relating to the Service will not exceed one hundred U.S. dollars
        ($100).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">10. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Service and request deletion of your account at any time. We may
        suspend or terminate access if you breach these Terms or if we discontinue the Service.
        Sections 5 through 9 survive termination.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">11. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected in the "Last
        updated" date above. Continued use of the Service after a change constitutes acceptance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to
        <%= mail_to @contact_email, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-500">
    See also our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" %>.
  </footer>
</article>
